1
00:00:00,588 --> 00:00:03,488
(Amy:)No, I had a cover story.
I told everyone it was herpes.

2
00:00:05,292 --> 00:00:09,492
- So how's everything with you and Leonard?
- I don't know. It's still kind of weird.

3
00:00:09,663 --> 00:00:13,103
(Penny:)We haven't really recovered
since he proposed to me in the middle of sex.

4
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:15,527
(Amy:)Oh. Boo-hoo.

5
00:00:16,103 --> 00:00:17,933
(Amy:)If Sheldon proposed to me during sex...

6
00:00:18,105 --> 00:00:20,805
...my ovaries would grab onto him
and never let go.

7
00:00:26,981 --> 00:00:30,381
(Sheldon:)Leonard, where do you stand
on the anthropic principle?

8
00:00:30,851 --> 00:00:34,841
- Interesting question. On the one hand...
- You don't even know what it is, do you?

9
00:00:35,823 --> 00:00:37,953
(Sheldon:)The anthropic principle states...

10
00:00:38,125 --> 00:00:42,065
(Sheldon:)...that if we wish to explain
why our universe exists the way it does...

11
00:00:42,229 --> 00:00:44,959
(Sheldon:)...the answer is that
it must have qualities...

12
00:00:45,132 --> 00:00:47,462
(Sheldon:)...that allow intelligent creatures
to arise...

13
00:00:47,635 --> 00:00:49,625
(Sheldon:)...who are capable of asking the question.

14
00:00:49,803 --> 00:00:53,133
(Sheldon:)As I am doing so eloquently right now.

15
00:00:54,108 --> 00:00:56,098
(Leonard:)I know what the anthropic principle is.

16
00:00:56,644 --> 00:00:58,474
(Sheldon:)Of course.
I just explained it to you.

17
00:00:59,847 --> 00:01:02,047
(Sheldon:)Now, where do you stand on it?

